WEBVTT

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:03.825
How to use: WildTrace in 2 minutes. The open atlas of illegal wildlife trade: three research questions, answered live.

00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:07.639
The Atlas: Every point is a seizure, arrest or conviction from public reports, graded by its evidence.

00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:10.251
The Atlas: Pulse sums up what is in view. Every row is a filter.

00:00:10.351 --> 00:00:16.207
Question 1 of 3: How strong is the evidence on pangolin cases in India?.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:20.521
Question 1: One search box for species, places and cases.

00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:30.517
Question 1: Each species: its CITES listing, trade names and where it is seized.

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:36.010
Question 1: Pangolin and India now filter the map, Pulse and timeline.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.880
Question 1: Each case: a plain account and its evidence grade.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:45.293
Question 1: Every source is listed with its outlet. Nobody accused is ever named.

00:00:45.393 --> 00:00:52.427
Question 2 of 3: Where does seized red sanders go, and through which hubs?.

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:57.360
Question 2: Flows: seized shipments reported to CITES, from source to market.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.262
Question 2: Pick a species. Lines shade from source region to market.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:09.128
Question 2: Evidence: what was seized, when, who reported it, and the news.

00:01:09.228 --> 00:01:15.898
Question 3 of 3: Do animal-borne outbreaks and trafficking overlap in Central Africa?.

00:01:15.998 --> 00:01:19.111
Question 3: Zoonoses: WHO outbreak reports beside the trade. A shared map, not a cause.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:25.367
Question 3: DR Congo, Uganda and Gabon lead outbreaks from wildlife contact.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:32.854
Question 3: Which traded species carry relatives of human viruses.

00:01:32.954 --> 00:01:41.144
Tools: Investigate: a link chart, plus your own data, kept in your browser.

00:01:41.244 --> 00:01:45.029
Tools: Analysis: the whole record on one sheet.

00:01:45.129 --> 00:01:47.436
Tools: Tours explain every section; switch them off any time.

00:01:47.536 --> 00:01:51.959
WildTrace: Open data, free to reuse. Download every case as CSV, cite it with DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22902819 · tarunv13.github.io/wildtrace
